oomd/overbudget — a declared budget is a policy the system acts on.

`memory = 4G` in a box profile becomes `podman --memory`, and rootless podman
on a machine with no systemd frequently has no cgroup delegation to enforce it
with: the flag is accepted and does nothing. KDOS does not offer a key it
cannot enforce, so THIS is the enforcement — a box over the budget its own
profile declared is preferred as a victim, ahead of the general rule that boxed
processes are preferred.

The tree is arranged so that only the budget can produce the right answer:

  arch          512M declared, 1.2 G held across cargo (600 M) and rustc (640 M)
  kdos-apps     nothing declared, firefox-esr at 480 M
  kdosbuild     a HOST process at 2 G — larger than anything in either box

Without the budget check the answer is kdosbuild, because the boxed preference
is not absolute and 2 G is more than twice 640 M. With it the answer is rustc:
the largest process of the box that broke its own promise.
